ot/issues/comments/3327254699","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110831#issuecomment-3327254699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110831","id":3327254699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GUeCr","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T08:45:07Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T08:45:07Z","body":"@nestorac Yes, but also see the linked PR for details why its creates such a difference between 4.4 and 4.5.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327254699/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3329699783","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110831#issuecomment-3329699783","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110831","id":3329699783,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Gdy_H","user":{"login":"rrbenx","id":7167857,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNjc4NTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7167857?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx","html_url":"https://github.com/rrbenx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrbenx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T16:07:42Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T16:07:42Z","body":"@smix8 sorry about bothering you, but I've been reading the different posts about navigation errors and the PR provided. All the messages are very confusing and I did the only thing pointed out which is setting navigation/3d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale to 0.001 and nothing happenend. So, you talk about \"unsolved errors\" but there is no further informaiton about how to solve this errors. My cuestion is: How is the optimal way to proceed in an scenario like the MRP provided (a large and complex landscape)? \n\nThanks in advance.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3329699783/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333384488","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110831#issuecomment-3333384488","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110831","id":3333384488,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Gr2ko","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T10:52:07Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T10:52:07Z","body":"@rrbenx The reason your project somehow works in 4.4.1 is because it continues trying to merge edges where it can after errors. In Godot 4.5 an error returns the function. Since your terrain baked navmesh geometry creates so many rasterization errors it returns very early so there are not pathfinding connections build for all those edges, hence its broken. That is what the linked PR tries to solve as it changes back that errors are no \"real errors\" so that it continue to merge what it can even if it is half broken.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333384488/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333573506","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110831#issuecom